tent/uploads/2012/11/img_4849.jpg?w=188" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4849.jpg?w=640" src="https://i0.wp.com/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4849.jpg?w=164&#038;h=262&#038;ssl=1" width="164" height="262" loading="lazy" data-original-width="164" data-original-height="262" itemprop="http://schema.org/image" title="IMG_4849" alt="IMG_4849" style="width: 164px; height: 262px;" /> </a> </div> </div> <!-- close group --> <div class="gallery-group images-1" style="width: 201px; height: 266px;" data-original-width="201" data-original-height="266" > <div class="tiled-gallery-item tiled-gallery-item-small" itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"> <a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/2012/11/18/australians-for-mussalaha-reconciliation-in-syria/img_4699/" border="0" itemprop="url"> <meta itemprop="width" content="197"> <meta itemprop="height" content="262"> <img class="" data-attachment-id="39" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4699.jpg" data-orig-size="768,1024" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;3.5&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;Picasa&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;Canon PowerShot G10&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1243572635&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;12.074&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;3200&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.025&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" data-image-title="IMG_4699" data-image-description="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4699.jpg?w=225" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4699.jpg?w=768" src="https://i0.wp.com/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/img_4699.jpg?w=197&#038;h=262&#038;ssl=1" width="197" height="262" loading="lazy" data-original-width="197" data-original-height="262" itemprop="http://schema.org/image" title="IMG_4699" alt="IMG_4699" style="width: 197px; height: 262px;" /> </a> </div> </div> <!-- close group --> <div class="gallery-group images-1" style="width: 238px; height: 266px;" data-original-width="238" data-original-height="266" > <div class="tiled-gallery-item tiled-gallery-item-small" itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"> <a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/2012/11/18/australians-for-mussalaha-reconciliation-in-syria/1-2008/" border="0" itemprop="url"> <meta itemprop="width" content="234"> <meta itemprop="height" content="262"> <img class="" data-attachment-id="26" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/1-2008.jpg" data-orig-size="2587,2900" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;5.6&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;Canon PowerShot G10&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1227704449&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;15.673&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;80&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.0025&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" data-image-title="1 2008" data-image-description="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/1-2008.jpg?w=268" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/1-2008.jpg?w=913" src="https://i0.wp.com/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/11/1-2008.jpg?w=234&#038;h=262&#038;ssl=1" width="234" height="262" loading="lazy" data-original-width="234" data-original-height="262" itemprop="http://schema.org/image" title="1 2008" alt="1 2008" style="width: 234px; height: 262px;" /> </a> </div> </div> <!-- close group --> </div> <!-- close row --> </div>
<p>They then talk about what happened to Ahmad after the start of the so-called Arab Spring in Syria and after Jess had left. Ahmad got a job as a truck driver and went to the “besieged city of Homs” because “he wanted to find out what was happening there”. At some point, Ahmad joined the militarized opposition and became a money runner, delivering 50,000 &#8211; 100,000 USD to fighters in the eastern suburbs of Damascus. Jess believes the money came from Saudi Arabia or Qatar. Ahmad claims he was a witness to a chemical attack on rebels and civilians in Damascus, asserting that 1,500 people died in the attack. Eventually, he tells us he fled Syria, taking 9 to 10 days to cross from the town of al-Zabadani into Lebanon.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Interwoven with the conversation between Jess and Ahmad are snippets from ABC news reports that date from the start of the crisis in Syria to more recent times. There are also verses read from a poem about Damascus written by a much-loved Syrian poet, Nizar Qabbani (1923 – 1998), who was a Syrian nationalist.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The extracts from ABC news reports serve to give credence to Ahmad’s view of events in Syria, and the poem softens the documentary nature of the program and aids in presenting Ahmad as a sympathetic figure; the poet’s yearning and love for Damascus could be understood to reflect that of Ahmad’s.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Jess Davis explains that she and Ahmad became ‘instant friends’ because of ‘his openness and friendly laugh’. Since virtually nothing is known about “Ahmad” except that he lived in Damascus when Jess met him, it is not possible for listeners to determine what motivates him to back insurgents funded by Saudi Arabia and Qatar. Jess doesn’t examine what Ahmad is prepared to do for his version of “freedom”; the political platform of his insurgent friends certainly wouldn’t attract the majority of Syrian women.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>What underlines the production of <em>The drawers of memory: Ahmad’s story</em> is the faith the ABC producer has in the credibility of one man whom she met on the street and who, she admits, was a money runner for insurgents. <strong>The program neither acknowledges nor gives a right of reply to Syrian civilians targeted by those insurgents, ‘ordinary Syrians’ who don’t support a foreign-backed militarized opposition that is fuelled by hatred and inspired by a particular school of Islam foreign to the majority of Muslims in Syria. </strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>After Ahmad joined the insurgents, Jess tells us he went to Jobar, in the eastern suburbs of Damascus. According to the Wikipedia page <em>Damascus Offensive (2013),</em> Jobar was the base from which armed groups launched a sustained offensive in early 2013, firing mortars into the suburbs of Damascus. Many Syrians were killed while going about their everyday business.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>In March 2013, a signatory of this letter received the following message from the son of a close Syrian friend.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<blockquote><p><em>hi Sue, </em></p>
<p><em> </em></p>
<p><em>just to tell you that mum returned to her maker yesterday in Damascus few meters from our place&#8230;. a mortar bomb fell on her &#8230;..</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>
<p>It is rare to hear the voices of these victims outside of Syria, but on 11 November 2013, an insurgent mortar attack on a suburb in Damascus killed four children from the St John of Damascus School and their bus driver, and BBC’s Lyse Doucet attended the funeral for two of the children and interviewed Rima Haddad, whose son had been a friend of one of the victims. The BBC reporter explains that Rima is ‘devastated, like so many here’. Clearly very distraught, Rima says on camera,</p>
<p><a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/complaint-to-the-bbc-regarding-panoramas-saving-syrias-children/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am/" rel="attachment wp-att-1169"><img data-attachment-id="1169" data-permalink="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/complaint-to-the-bbc-regarding-panoramas-saving-syrias-children/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am/" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg" data-orig-size="1272,835" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;Picasa&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1400874120&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;}" data-image-title="Fullscreen capture 24052014 54200 AM" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=960" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-1169" src="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=960&#038;h=630" alt="Fullscreen capture 24052014 54200 AM"   srcset="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=500 500w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=1000 1000w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=150 150w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=300 300w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/fullscreen-capture-24052014-54200-am.jpg?w=768 768w" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /></a></p>
<blockquote><p><em>What did they do to die like this, by some bombs from dirty people? Please tell America, please tell Britain, Turkey, Qatar, Saudi Arabia that they are bad people. (Ref: </em><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9HIGTpvfRPg"><em>Damascus mortar attack Children and bus driver buried</em></a><em>)</em></p></blockquote>
<p><em> </em></p>
<div class="tiled-gallery type-square tiled-gallery-unresized" data-original-width="960" data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:42733181,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org\/abcs-editorial-stance-on-syria-contradicts-beliefs-and-values-of-australians\/&quot;,&quot;likes_blog_id&quot;:42733181}' itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageGallery" > <div class="gallery-row" style="width: 960px; height: 480px;" data-original-width="960" data-original-height="480" > <div class="gallery-group" style="width: 480px; height: 480px;" data-original-width="480" data-original-height="480" > <div class="tiled-gallery-item " itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"> <a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/abcs-editorial-stance-on-syria-contradicts-beliefs-and-values-of-australians/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-21-10-pm/" border="0" itemprop="url"> <meta itemprop="width" content="476"> <meta itemprop="height" content="476"> <img class="" data-attachment-id="2032" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-21-10-pm.jpg" data-orig-size="580,365" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;Picasa&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1452054078&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.21.10 pm" data-image-description="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-21-10-pm.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-21-10-pm.jpg?w=580" src="https://i0.wp.com/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-21-10-pm.jpg?w=476&#038;h=476&#038;crop=1&#038;ssl=1" width="476" height="476" loading="lazy" data-original-width="476" data-original-height="476" itemprop="http://schema.org/image" title="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.21.10 pm" alt="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.21.10 pm" style="width: 476px; height: 476px;" /> </a> </div> </div> <div class="gallery-group" style="width: 480px; height: 480px;" data-original-width="480" data-original-height="480" > <div class="tiled-gallery-item " itemprop="associatedMedia" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject"> <a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/abcs-editorial-stance-on-syria-contradicts-beliefs-and-values-of-australians/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-22-42-pm/" border="0" itemprop="url"> <meta itemprop="width" content="476"> <meta itemprop="height" content="476"> <img class="" data-attachment-id="2033" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-22-42-pm.jpg" data-orig-size="568,360" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;Picasa&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1452054168&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.22.42 pm" data-image-description="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-22-42-pm.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-22-42-pm.jpg?w=568" src="https://i0.wp.com/australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2016-01-06-at-3-22-42-pm.jpg?w=476&#038;h=476&#038;crop=1&#038;ssl=1" width="476" height="476" loading="lazy" data-original-width="476" data-original-height="476" itemprop="http://schema.org/image" title="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.22.42 pm" alt="Screen Shot 2016-01-06 at 3.22.42 pm" style="width: 476px; height: 476px;" /> </a> </div> </div> </div> </div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>A day before the children’s and bus driver’s death, another mortar fired by insurgents killed Girgis Elias and his four children Eli, Tala, Peter and Nirvana when they were in their car in the district of Kashkool, Damascus. (Ref: <a href="http://orontes.jimdo.com/2013/11/12/just-another-family/"><em>Just another Family</em></a><em>) </em>Another signatory of this letter, a Syrian refugee now living in Australia, was a friend of this family. <strong>An ABC audience might expect substantial weight to be given the accounts of such Syrians in Australia. However, this <em>Earshot</em> program provides no reference to their stories or perspective, thus breaching the ABC Codes of Practice that relate to impartiality. </strong></p>
<p><strong> </strong></p>
<p><strong>Jess doesn’t ask Ahmad why he believes the random targeting and killing of these citizens will take the country forward to ‘freedom’. An ABC audience might rightly expect she would. </strong></p>
<p><strong> </strong></p>
<p style="text-align:center;"><strong>________________________________________________</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/abcs-editorial-stance-on-syria-contradicts-beliefs-and-values-of-australians/screen-shot-2015-12-025/" rel="attachment wp-att-1999"><br />
<img data-attachment-id="1999" data-permalink="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/abcs-editorial-stance-on-syria-contradicts-beliefs-and-values-of-australians/screen-shot-2015-12-025/" data-orig-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg" data-orig-size="613,446" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;Picasa&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1450973216&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Screen Shot 2015-12-025" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=300" data-large-file="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=613" class="aligncenter size-large wp-image-1999" src="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=960&#038;h=698" alt="Screen Shot 2015-12-025"   srcset="https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=500 500w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=150 150w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg?w=300 300w, https://australiansforreconciliationinsyria.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/screen-shot-2015-12-025.jpg 613w" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /></a></p>
<p><em>Image: screenshot taken from </em><em><a href="http://www.ft.com/intl/cms/s/0/683d7c5a-c0c8-11e4-9949-00144feab7de.html#slide0">article by Erika Solomon</a>, 3 March 2015</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>WHAT TO CALL AHMAD’S ‘FREEDOM’ FIGHTERS?</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>A hallmark of ABC reporting on the war in Syria has been the use of labels to designate the different players. If not used with discretion, labels can present the conflict as a football game. This <em>Earshot</em> program lines up two ‘teams’: “the brutal regime”; “the Assad regime”; and “pro-government militiamen” <em>versus</em> Ahmad, “a fighter for the Free Syrian Army” and “an opposition activist”. Ahmad’s side certainly sounds more benign. However, there is no reference in the program to the Syrian national army; Syrian women; or the vast majority of Syrians who oppose a militarized opposition.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
